WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- So have y'all met before?

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.499
Have you ever met Tim?

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:03.533
I didn't know if y'all met before.

00:00:03.533 --> 00:00:04.366
- Just backstage.

00:00:04.366 --> 00:00:05.389
- [Kelly] Just backstage?

00:00:05.389 --> 00:00:06.222
- Yeah

00:00:06.222 --> 00:00:07.055
But not before that.

00:00:07.055 --> 00:00:08.730
Like, "Oh, okay. Right on. Right on."

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.590
So I wanna talk about your new book.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.240
So your new book is
called The Wind at My Back

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.620
which is such a beautiful title.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.680
And this picture, by the
way, what a great cover.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.513
- And that-

00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:18.549
- It says so much

00:00:18.549 --> 00:00:19.382
- That moment too. That moment-

00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:20.215
- Yeah.

00:00:20.215 --> 00:00:21.990
- Like it was the first time

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.950
that I was performing Swan Lake

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.980
at the Metropolitan Opera House.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.500
And Raven Wilkinson never had
the opportunity to perform

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.150
on that stage as a black woman.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.070
- But you see that in
your face in this picture.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.590
- And she came on stage
and brought me the flowers

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.560
and it's tradition in
ballet that it's only men

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.360
that bring the flowers and the ushers.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.060
So we fought to have this
black woman come on stage.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.460
You should have been on
that stage performing

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.380
and present those flowers to me.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.213
- Yeah.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.660
- And I just like crumbled

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.220
because it was a surprise.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.920
And I like knelt down
and gave her the flowers

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:53.753
and she picked me up

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.410
and she was like, "Nope, take them back."

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.430
These are yours.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.450
- Yeah.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.320
I love that though.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.420
It's just the, I don't know

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.984
the expression on your face in
this picture says everything.

00:01:02.984 --> 00:01:05.290
- It was like tears and
love and joy and everything.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.530
- Yeah. Admiration. It's
just like all there.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.363
It's very beautiful.

00:01:08.363 --> 00:01:09.196
- Thank you.

00:01:09.196 --> 00:01:10.029
- I love that it's the cover.

00:01:10.029 --> 00:01:10.862
- Thank you.

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:11.695
- Can you tell us a little about the book?

00:01:11.695 --> 00:01:13.320
Like why you felt it
was necessary to write?

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.153
- Yeah.

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:17.280
So, you know, I wouldn't
be where I am if it weren't

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.498
for the incredible women in my life.

00:01:19.498 --> 00:01:22.020
Mentors in my life, and then Raven coming

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.120
into my life at such a critical time.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.740
I was still a soloist at A.B.T

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.750
and really struggling to find my voice

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.430
and place as a black woman.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.270
- Yeah.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.380
- In the ballet world.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.760
And seeing her, you know, she
literally walked in my path

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.280
and my footsteps or I walk in hers.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.113
- Yeah.

00:01:39.113 --> 00:01:40.500
- But, you know, 50 years prior

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.350
and just also to see
how much hasn't changed

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.430
in the valley world

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.853
from 50 years ago and what
Raven had experienced.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.760
I just felt it was
important for, you know,

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.033
again to see this,

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.870
the power of intergenerational
relationships

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.490
and the importance of mentorship

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:00.300
and having those relationships
with your elders.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.920
And so it's a story of
Raven's life and my life

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.240
and how they come together.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.610
And I don't think I would
be a principal dancer.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:12.540
I would be here without the
relationship that we built

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.790
and the friendship that, you know,

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:17.250
we had she passed a
couple of years ago now,

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:21.000
but she just made such
a big impact on my life

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.250
and showed, gave me a bigger purpose

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.240
of what it is I'm doing.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.820
Like it wasn't just about
striving to be a principal dancer.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.653
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:27.653 --> 00:02:28.486
- But it was being an example

00:02:28.486 --> 00:02:31.290
and representation on
the stage for so many

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.520
- And a hero.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.250
And it's kinda sad now that you say that.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.780
Like, I didn't really put that together

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.340
but you just mentioned the two of you

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.590
'cause you're like there's
still not a big presence.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:41.423
- No.

00:02:41.423 --> 00:02:42.780
- And that's a shame.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.613
- It is, yeah.

00:02:43.613 --> 00:02:45.420
And I mean, it's so important, you know

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.660
that beyond the stage that I have a voice

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.269
and that I use my platform to-

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:51.102
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:51.102 --> 00:02:51.935
- To kind of get out there and

00:02:51.935 --> 00:02:54.120
and to share, you know,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.490
the ballet world,

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:57.570
bring it to more people

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.330
and try and bring more diversity to it.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.190
But through my own
foundation that I've started

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.560
a program called the Be Bold program

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.630
and it's free ballet classes

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.940
and the afterschool space
at Boys and Girls Clubs

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.500
in the Bronx is where we're starting.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.435
- Yeah.

00:03:11.435 --> 00:03:12.690
- So it's, it, yes.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:13.523
Looking back

00:03:13.523 --> 00:03:16.350
and giving opportunity

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.270
is so important for me.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.100
- Yeah. Well it surely was.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:20.933
Look at that picture.

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:21.766
- Yeah.

00:03:21.766 --> 00:03:23.400
- Well, speaking of dance

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.170
have y'all ever done like
a father daughter dance?

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.133
Have y'all done that?

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:26.966
[Both] Yes.

00:03:26.966 --> 00:03:27.799
- I love that.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.190
- This is a strange,
comedically I've been looking

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.690
at the way the world is and

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.869
because of the staff of Santa Claus,

00:03:35.869 --> 00:03:36.900
my family,

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.720
my niece Jess is a dancer

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.910
and I don't know much about it.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.980
My wife was a dancer and I want-

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.000
- Yeah.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.833
- I'm just not into it.

00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:48.150
I mean, comedy, I mean,
most dancing comedians

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.910
get is burlesque, which
is a form of dance.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.190
And then I got into
this thing about ballet

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.510
and I don't understand it,

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.640
but between all it makes
me emotional to think

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.430
that this art form is an expression

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.010
of beauty through the body.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:05.370
And they do it no matter
whether there's money

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.870
or attraction to it at all.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.241
It's such an honorable thing,

00:04:08.241 --> 00:04:11.190
now I'm a huge fan of ballet that they-

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.191
- Yeah, so so disciplined.

00:04:13.191 --> 00:04:14.024
- Yeah.

00:04:14.024 --> 00:04:17.100
- Well the the comedy
part is the worst dictator

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.530
in the world, Stalin,
murdered millions of people.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.000
This, but not the dancers.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:21.833
- Not-

00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:22.666
- Something-

00:04:22.666 --> 00:04:23.762
- There was a line, he had a line.

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:24.780
- Something to do with the
communists, they love it.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.550
But I, my heart went out

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.830
to the people that produced this stuff

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.010
and all of our bad times, but especially

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.950
fine orchestras and then
dancers, people that do that.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.770
And you, I'm just amazed
at what you people do

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.730
and how you express it.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.394
It's art and love and design and movement.

00:04:41.394 --> 00:04:43.506
- Beautiful. See your
body going like that.

00:04:43.506 --> 00:04:45.240
And that's so cool that y'all
get to do the Father daughter.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.650
I thought that was really special.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.000
- Well what, book did we tell that,

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.080
remember that book you read?

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.940
- Yeah, it was literally
called Misty Copeland.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:53.100
I had a book that I read when I was like-

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.645
- Just saw it backstage and the
look on her face, she's like

00:04:55.645 --> 00:04:57.360
- I was like, "Oh."

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.930
- Oh my gosh, it's so funny.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.030
We didn't know that.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.280
- Every morning like I
would, I was, I don't know

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.460
probably like seven or
eight years old and my mom

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.420
and I, we used to read books

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.430
like while she was making breakfast

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.290
and I had, it was just like,
you know, picture books

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.220
like a kid's picture book.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.080
But I read it every morning like-

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:13.913
- Oh my god.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:14.746
- Every morning.

00:05:14.746 --> 00:05:17.307
So when I heard, I was like, "Who?"

00:05:18.629 --> 00:05:19.800
- Right next to her?

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.533
Just take it in, take it in.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.360
Ah, Misty's book is called

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.840
The Wind at My Back: Resilience
Grace and Other Gifts

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.850
for My Mentor Raven Wilkinson.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.750
It's out now y'all gotta check it out.

